:: Fishing Combat Coast Path
<<effects>>
<<run fishingCombatEffects()>>

/* Player orgasm */
<<if $arousal gte $arousalmax>>
	<<fishCombatCoastPathOrgasm>>

/* You've caught the fish */
<<elseif $fishing.combat.fishDistance lte 0>>
	<<if Time.dayState is "day" and random(1, 15) is 1 and $daily.fishing.seagullSteal is undefined>>
		<<fishingSeagullCaught "coastPath">>
	<<else>>
		<<fishCombatCoastPathCaught>>
	<</if>>

/* Your line has snapped */
<<elseif $fishing.combat.lineHealth lte 0>>
	<<fishCombatCoastPathLineSnapped>>

/* Still fishing */
<<else>>
	<<fishCombatCoastPathMain>>

<</if>>


:: Fishing Coast Path Cut Line
<<run endFishingCombat()>>
You release the tension on the rod, letting the line go slack. The <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> pulls harder, and with a sudden snap, the line breaks free. It disappears into the surf below.
<br><br>

<<link [[Re-hook the line and cast back out (0:03)|Fishing Coast Path Wait]]>><<pass 3>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Leave|Fishing Coast Path Approach]]>><</link>>


:: Widgets Fishing Combat Coast Path [widget]
<<widget "fishCombatCoastPathMain">>
	<<run fishCombatAction()>>
	<<fishCombatActionDescription>>
	<<printFishInfo>>
	<br><br>

	<<fishCombatActions "Coast Path">>
	<<fishingCoastPathCombatDebugLinks>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishCombatCoastPathCaught">>
	<<set _canEatFish to canEatFishTf($fishingHookedFish)>>
	<<run updateFishRecord($fishingHookedFish.type, $fishingHookedFish.size, "coastPath")>>
	<<run endFishingCombat()>>
	<<run holdCaughtFish($fishingHookedFish.type)>>

	<<fishingCatchFishText "coastPath">>
	<br><br>

	<<if _canEatFish>>
		It's such a small fish, you could probably fit the whole thing in your mouth.
		<br><br>
	<</if>>

	<<link [["Throw the " + $fishingHookedFish.type + " back"|Fishing Coast Path Throw Back]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Stow it away|Fishing Coast Path Keep]]>><</link>>
	<<if _canEatFish>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Eat the fish|Fishing Coast Path Cat Eat]]>><</link>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishCombatCoastPathLineSnapped">>
	Your line suddenly goes slack, and the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> disappears into the surf.
	<<run endFishingCombat()>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Re-hook the line and cast back out (0:03)|Fishing Coast Path Wait]]>><<pass 3>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave|Fishing Coast Path Approach]]>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishCombatCoastPathOrgasm">>
	<<orgasmFishingCoastPath>>
	The rod slips from your grip and the line goes slack, the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> has taken its chance and is gone.
	<<run endFishingCombat()>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Next|Fishing Coast Path Wait]]>><</link>>
<</widget>>
